// A function whose cases leave a gap, for tests/run.sh's `mutscore` section:
// 10 is above the line and 3 below it, but nothing pins where the line is, so
// moving it from > 9 to >= 9 goes unnoticed. Every other mutant fails a case:
// the line moved to 10, the weight changed or its operator swapped, the result
// forced to 0 or to 1. The weight is read after the comparison so that forcing
// the result still leaves `r` read: a mutant that left it unread would be
// refused by the compiler (E0410) instead of killed by a case.
big(int n) {
  int r = n > 9;
  r = r * 5;
} return int r;
(10):(5)
(3):(0)
